# PUT /api/sheets/{sheetId}/settings — save the sheet's settings. Body {"clerkLimit":"1.50","floor":"1.00","terms":"14","latePct":"0.00"}:
# amounts and the late percent with up to two decimals, kept with two; terms a whole number of days. A blank clerk limit is no
# limit (left as it is when a floor, terms or late percent are saved with it); a blank or missing floor, terms or late percent is left as it is.
# "policyDate" and "periodNumberingFrom" are yyyy-mm-dd dates: missing is left as it is, blank is none (off).
# "cap" is an amount with up to two decimals, kept with two: missing is left as it is, blank is none. Anything else is refused with 400
# and nothing is stored. Every saved setting is audited, even the value already in force, then the
# ROLLUP and TOTALS lines of the figures the floor moved.
# "from" gives, by setting key, the from-date (yyyy-mm-dd) a dated setting (clerk-limit, floor, terms, terms-<grade>, late-pct, cap) is
# recorded from; blank or missing: the sheet's today. A value already recorded from that date is replaced.
